## 5. Subsystem Deep-Dives

### 5.1 A-Z Discovered Repositories Bar Subsystem
- When the webview initializes, all discovered workspace repositories and folders are sorted alphabetically by folder name (`repos.sort((a, b) => a.name.localeCompare(b.name))`).
- Each repository renders as a compact checkbox chip in the main header:
  ```html
  <label class="repo-chip">
    <input type="checkbox" data-path="/path/to/repo" checked />
    <span class="repo-name">repo-name</span>
  </label>
  ```
- Unchecking a chip sets `pane.isHidden = true` and updates the layout immediately.
- Checking an inactive chip unhides the existing pane or spawns a new pane mapped to that repository root if one does not already exist.

### 5.2 Two-Row Pane Header Layout Subsystem
- **Row 1**:
  - `drag-handle` (`:::`): Grab handle for HTML5 drag-and-drop reordering.
  - `pane-number`: `#1`, `#2`, etc.
  - `pane-title`: Clickable title or compact dropdown to inspect/switch folder path.
  - `pane-actions`: Inline buttons `[⏮ 1st]`, `[◀]`, `[▶]`, and `[✕]`.
- **Row 2**:
  - VS Code Find input container holding the text box and the 3 action toggle badges (`Aa`, `ab`, `.*`).

### 5.3 Vanilla VS Code Search Widget Engine (`Aa`, `ab`, `.*`)
- **Match Case (`Aa`)**:
  - Inactive: Case-insensitive search (`filename.toLowerCase().includes(query.toLowerCase())`).
  - Active: Strict case-sensitive match (`filename.includes(query)`).
- **Match Whole Word (`ab`)**:
  - Escapes special characters, constructs regex boundary `\b${query}\b`.
  - Filename matches only if the target is a discrete word boundary.
- **Regular Expression (`.*`)**:
  - Constructs `new RegExp(pattern, flags)`.
  - Flags set to `g` (or `gi` when `Aa` is off).
  - If syntax is invalid, adds `.input-error` class to the input container (displaying VS Code error border color) and ignores corrupt regex until corrected.

